camchrome: a persona's local() fallback only accepts a clone that renders Latin.

1019 made local() find clones by full name, which also loaded the complex-script Windows faces
(Javanese Text, Leelawadee UI, MV Boli, Sylfaen, ...) through Noto clones that have no Latin
glyphs. Requested as a font-family they cannot change Latin text, so the face loaded by name but
was invisible to layout (Clearcote audit: "a Windows face that loads by name is also visible to
text layout"). The fallback now rejects a clone without a glyph for "a"; those faces are absent
both ways, as before 1019, while Calibri/Cambria and the other Latin clones still load.

--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/fonts/font_cache.cc
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/fonts/font_cache.cc
@@ -1095,6 +1095,14 @@
            {name + " Regular", compact + "-Regular", compact}) {
         uniquely_identified_font = unique_name_lookup->MatchUniqueName(
             String::FromUtf8(base::as_byte_span(candidate)));
+        // camchrome (1020): only a clone that renders basic Latin. A script-only clone (Noto
+        // Sans Javanese for Javanese Text) loading through local() while the same face as a
+        // font-family cannot change Latin text is a contradiction Windows never shows; such
+        // faces stay absent both ways.
+        if (uniquely_identified_font &&
+            uniquely_identified_font->unicharToGlyph('a') == 0) {
+          uniquely_identified_font = nullptr;
+        }
         if (uniquely_identified_font)
           break;
       }
@@ -1111,6 +1119,14 @@
            {clone, clone + " Regular", compact + "-Regular", compact}) {
         uniquely_identified_font = unique_name_lookup->MatchUniqueName(
             String::FromUtf8(base::as_byte_span(candidate)));
+        // camchrome (1020): only a clone that renders basic Latin. A script-only clone (Noto
+        // Sans Javanese for Javanese Text) loading through local() while the same face as a
+        // font-family cannot change Latin text is a contradiction Windows never shows; such
+        // faces stay absent both ways.
+        if (uniquely_identified_font &&
+            uniquely_identified_font->unicharToGlyph('a') == 0) {
+          uniquely_identified_font = nullptr;
+        }
         if (uniquely_identified_font)
           break;
       }
